From 617b40ddc9f5ed6e9142ce172232b80b7a10f6e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woodenwillis <william.b@millpex.org>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:21:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] tensor-g4: describe the S2MPUs as kernel devices

Add the 29 google,s2mpu-v9 nodes from the caiman vendor DTB
(BP1A.250505.005; reg, interrupts, and the always-on / deny-all /
off-at-boot flags) and list them all in seL4,kernel-devices, so the
kernel owns every S2MPU and no userspace component can be given one.

Each instance maps 0x5000, which covers every register the v9 driver
uses (through L1ENTRY_ATTR(7,63) at 0x4ffc); the kernel device window
is a single 2 MiB page table and cannot hold 29 full 64 KiB blocks.
The remaining 0xb000 of each block is reserved, not mapped.

No code touches the S2MPUs yet.
---
 src/plat/tensor-g4/overlay-tensor-g4.dts |  31 +++-
 tools/dts/tensor-g4.dts                  | 181 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 tools/hardware.yml                       |  11 ++
 3 files changed, 222 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/plat/tensor-g4/overlay-tensor-g4.dts b/src/plat/tensor-g4/overlay-tensor-g4.dts
index f33b7f1f7..b12545e42 100644
--- a/src/plat/tensor-g4/overlay-tensor-g4.dts
+++ b/src/plat/tensor-g4/overlay-tensor-g4.dts
@@ -11,7 +11,36 @@
